<law>
	<structure>
		<unit label="title" identifier="15.2" level="1">Counties, Cities and Towns</unit>
		<unit label="subtitle" identifier="II" level="2">Powers of Local Government</unit>
		<unit label="chapter" identifier="14" level="3">Governing Bodies of Localities</unit>
		<unit label="article" identifier="2" level="4">Meetings of Governing Bodies</unit>
	</structure>
	<section_number>15.2-1417</section_number>
	<catch_line>Special meetings</catch_line>
	<text>
		The governing body may also hold such special meetings, as it deems necessary, at such times and places as it finds convenient. It may adjourn such special meetings from time to time as it finds convenient and necessary.
	</text>
	<history>Code 1950, § 15-242; 1962, c. 623, § 15.1-537; 1997, c. 587.</history>
</law>
